helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153524	8			0	kid	z8bunh‖This function is intended for use in situations where the default Basic to Uno type converting mechanism is insufficient. This can happen when you try to access generic Any based interfaces, such as XPropertySet::setPropertyValue( Name, Value ) or X???Container::insertBy???( ???, Value ), from $[officename] Basic. The Basic runtime does not recognize these types as they are only defined in the corresponding service.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366	9			0	kid	hutdt]‖In this type of situation, $[officename] Basic chooses the best matching type for the Basic type that you want to convert. However, if the wrong type is selected, an error occurs. You use the CreateUnoValue() function to create a value for the unknown Uno type.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150769	10			0	kid	mf9g0b‖You can also use this function to pass non-Any values, but this is not recommend. If Basic already knows the target type, using the CreateUnoValue() function will only lead to additional converting operations that slow down the Basic execution.				20130829 23:02:48
