helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151193	46			0	kid	diglne‖Long integer variables range from -2147483648 to 2147483647. If you assign a floating-point value to a long integer variable, the decimal places are rounded to the next integer. Long integer variables are rapidly calculated in procedures and are suitable for counter variables in loops for large values. A long integer variable requires four bytes of memory. "&" is the type-declaration character.				20130829 23:02:48
