helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150953	55			0	kid	x7a-08‖Double variables can take positive or negative values ranging from 1.79769313486232 x 10E308 to 4.94065645841247 x 10E-324. Double variables are floating-point variables, in which the decimal precision decreases as the non-decimal part of the number increases. Double variables are suitable for precise calculations. Calculations require more time than for Single variables. A Double variable requires 8 bytes of memory. The type-declaration character is "#".				20130829 23:02:48
