helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3156320	196			0	kid	q-hgux‖            \<item type=\"input\"\>{=COLUMN(B2:B7)}\</item\> and \<item type=\"input\"\>=COLUMN(B2:B7)\</item\> both return 2 because the reference only contains column B as the second column in the table. Because single-column areas have only one column number, it does not make a difference whether or not the formula is used as an array formula.				20130829 23:02:48
