helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153152	87			0	kid	1hxz27‖VLOOKUP				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149984	88			0	kid	bg0u1b‖\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SVERWEIS\"\>Vertical search with reference to adjacent cells to the right.\</ahelp\> This function checks if a specific value is contained in the first column of an array. The function then returns the value in the same row of the column named by \<item type=\"literal\"\>Index\</item\>. If the \<item type=\"literal\"\>SortOrder\</item\> parameter is omitted or set to TRUE or one, it is assumed that the data is sorted in ascending order. In this case, if the exact \<item type=\"literal\"\>SearchCriterion\</item\> is not found, the last value that is smaller than the criterion will be returned. If \<item type=\"literal\"\>SortOrder\</item\> is set to FALSE or zero, an exact match must be found, otherwise the error \<emph\>Error: Value Not Available\</emph\> will be the result. Thus with a value of zero the data does not need to be sorted in ascending order.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146898	89			0	kid	we14=j‖Syntax				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150156	90			0	kid	9[ez[-‖=VLOOKUP(SearchCriterion; Array; Index; SortOrder)				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149289	91			0	kid	3kqsoq‖            \<emph\>SearchCriterion\</emph\> is the value searched for in the first column of the array.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153884	92			0	kid	bauzv3‖            \<emph\>Array\</emph\> is the reference, which is to comprise at least two columns.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3156005	93			0	kid	6pvmgb‖            \<emph\>Index\</emph\> is the number of the column in the array that contains the value to be returned. The first column has the number 1.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3151208	94			0	kid	pxveny‖            \<emph\>SortOrder\</emph\> is an optional parameter that indicates whether the first column in the array is sorted in ascending order. Enter the Boolean value FALSE or zero if the first column is not sorted in ascending order. Sorted columns can be searched much faster and the function always returns a value, even if the search value was not matched exactly, if it is between the lowest and highest value of the sorted list. In unsorted lists, the search value must be matched exactly. Otherwise the function will return this message: \<emph\>Error: Value Not Available\</emph\>.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147487	95			0	kid	hlkm8h‖Example				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154129	96			0	kid	5[t2r9‖You want to enter the number of a dish on the menu in cell A1, and the name of the dish is to appear as text in the neighboring cell (B1) immediately. The Number to Name assignment is contained in the D1:E100 array. D1 contains \<item type=\"input\"\>100\</item\>, E1 contains the name \<item type=\"input\"\>Vegetable Soup\</item\>, and so forth, for 100 menu items. The numbers in column D are sorted in ascending order; thus, the optional \<item type=\"literal\"\>SortOrder\</item\> parameter is not necessary.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3145663	97			0	kid	kvg89+‖Enter the following formula in B1:				20130829 23:02:48
