helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149200	99			0	kid	0gf[py‖As soon as you enter a number in A1 B1 will show the corresponding text contained in the second column of reference D1:E100. Entering a nonexistent number displays the text with the next number down. To prevent this, enter FALSE as the last parameter in the formula so that an error message is generated when a nonexistent number is entered.				20130829 23:02:48
