helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149336	105			0	kid	c[y9bd‖            \<emph\>SearchCriterion\</emph\> is the value which is to be searched for in the single-row or single-column array.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3159167	106			0	kid	d5x]zc‖            \<emph\>LookupArray\</emph\> is the reference searched. A lookup array can be a single row or column, or part of a single row or column.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147239	107			0	kid	n-76ru‖            \<emph\>Type\</emph\> may take the values 1, 0, or -1. If Type = 1 or if this optional parameter is missing, it is assumed that the first column of the search array is sorted in ascending order. If Type = -1 it is assumed that the column in sorted in descending order. This corresponds to the same function in Microsoft Excel.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154265	231			0	kid	bws6-j‖If Type = 0, only exact matches are found. If the search criterion is found more than once, the function returns the index of the first matching value. Only if Type = 0 can you search for regular expressions.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3147528	232			0	kid	z]5wjx‖If Type = 1 or the third parameter is missing, the index of the last value that is smaller or equal to the search criterion is returned. This applies even when the search array is not sorted. For Type = -1, the first value that is larger or equal is returned.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155119	108			0	kid	twu1qk‖Example				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3155343	109			0	kid	uo7v3q‖            \<item type=\"input\"\>=MATCH(200;D1:D100)\</item\> searches the area D1:D100, which is sorted by column D, for the value 200. As soon as this value is reached, the number of the row in which it was found is returned. If a higher value is found during the search in the column, the number of the previous row is returned.				20130829 23:02:48
