helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id7439802				0	kid	xmbfu0‖            \<item type=\"input\"\>=OFFSET(B2:C3;1;1)\</item\> returns a reference to B2:C3 moved down by 1 row and one column to the right (C3:D4).				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3009430				0	kid	o91f9w‖            \<item type=\"input\"\>=OFFSET(B2:C3;-1;-1)\</item\> returns a reference to B2:C3 moved up by 1 row and one column to the left (A1:B2).				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id2629169				0	kid	mrv4br‖            \<item type=\"input\"\>=OFFSET(B2:C3;0;0;3;4)\</item\> returns a reference to B2:C3 resized to 3 rows and 4 columns (B2:E4).				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id6668599				0	kid	pbfueq‖            \<item type=\"input\"\>=OFFSET(B2:C3;1;0;3;4)\</item\> returns a reference to B2:C3 moved down by one row resized to 3 rows and 4 columns (B2:E4).				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153739	122			0	kid	k67d+5‖            \<item type=\"input\"\>=SUM(OFFSET(A1;2;2;5;6))\</item\> determines the total of the area that starts in cell C3 and has a height of 5 rows and a width of 6 columns (area=C3:H7).				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159273				0	kid	p+i-=v‖\<bookmark_value\>LOOKUP function\</bookmark_value\>				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159273	123			0	kid	64o9ex‖LOOKUP				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3153389	124			0	kid	ku3qnx‖\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VERWEIS\"\>Returns the contents of a cell either from a one-row or one-column range.\</ahelp\> Optionally, the assigned value (of the same index) is returned in a different column and row. As opposed to \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060109.xhp\" name=\"VLOOKUP\"\>VLOOKUP\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060109.xhp\" name=\"HLOOKUP\"\>HLOOKUP\</link\>, search and result vector may be at different positions; they do not have to be adjacent. Additionally, the search vector for the LOOKUP must be sorted ascending, otherwise the search will not return any usable results.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id4484084				0	kid	t6pqb1‖If LOOKUP cannot find the search criterion, it matches the largest value in the search vector that is less than or equal to the search criterion.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152947	125			0	kid	6vzhwx‖Syntax				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154104	126			0	kid	z5-y04‖LOOKUP(SearchCriterion; SearchVector; ResultVector)				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150646	127			0	kid	ki7[r6‖            \<emph\>SearchCriterion\</emph\> is the value to be searched for; entered either directly or as a reference.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3154854	128			0	kid	44vi8d‖            \<emph\>SearchVector\</emph\> is the single-row or single-column area to be searched.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149925	129			0	kid	l6g59[‖            \<emph\>ResultVector\</emph\> is another single-row or single-column range from which the result of the function is taken. The result is the cell of the result vector with the same index as the instance found in the search vector.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148624	130			0	kid	f=2w=f‖Example				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149809	131			0	kid	qg8+fr‖            \<item type=\"input\"\>=LOOKUP(A1;D1:D100;F1:F100)\</item\> searches the corresponding cell in range D1:D100 for the number you entered in A1. For the instance found, the index is determined, for example, the 12th cell in this range. Then, the contents of the 12th cell are returned as the value of the function (in the result vector).				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149425				0	kid	a44]1y‖\<bookmark_value\>STYLE function\</bookmark_value\>				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149425	133			0	kid	1pdqes‖STYLE				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150826	134			0	kid	8dc7hc‖\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VORLAGE\"\>Applies a style to the cell containing the formula.\</ahelp\> After a set amount of time, another style can be applied. This function always returns the value 0, allowing you to add it to another function without changing the value. Together with the CURRENT function you can apply a color to a cell regardless of the value. For example: =...+STYLE(IF(CURRENT()>3;"red";"green")) applies the style "red" to the cell if the value is greater than 3, otherwise the style "green" is applied. Both cell formats have to be defined beforehand.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145373	135			0	kid	d647y8‖Syntax				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149302	136			0	kid	7h-sqn‖STYLE("Style"; Time; "Style2")				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3150596	137			0	kid	l+3[7k‖            \<emph\>Style\</emph\> is the name of a cell style assigned to the cell. Style names must be entered in quotation marks.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3156149	138			0	kid	niu2mk‖            \<emph\>Time\</emph\> is an optional time range in seconds. If this parameter is missing the style will not be changed after a certain amount of time has passed.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149520	139			0	kid	m==jt5‖            \<emph\>Style2\</emph\> is the optional name of a cell style assigned to the cell after a certain amount of time has passed. If this parameter is missing "Default" is assumed.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_idN111CA				0	kid	87ljck‖            \<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>         				20130829 23:02:48
