helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id909451				0	kid	4gipo3‖Two different syntax definitions can be used:				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id1665089				0	kid	9b[1lz‖GETPIVOTDATA(TargetField; pivot table; [ Field 1; Item 1; ... ])				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id4997100				0	kid	pqt8p4‖GETPIVOTDATA(pivot table; Constraints)				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id1672109				0	kid	pw1qb0‖The second syntax is assumed if exactly two parameters are given, of which the first parameter is a cell or cell range reference. The first syntax is assumed in all other cases. The Function Wizard shows the first syntax.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id9464094				0	kid	o3u40d‖First Syntax				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id9302346				0	kid	09x9[n‖            \<emph\>TargetField\</emph\> is a string that selects one of the pivot table's data fields. The string can be the name of the source column, or the data field name as shown in the table (like "Sum - Sales").				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id8296151				0	kid	+]a=u4‖            \<emph\>pivot table\</emph\> is a reference to a cell or cell range that is positioned within a pivot table or contains a pivot table. If the cell range contains several pivot tables, the table that was created last is used.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id4809411				0	kid	8tnlp+‖If no \<emph\>Field n / Item n\</emph\> pairs are given, the grand total is returned. Otherwise, each pair adds a constraint that the result must satisfy. \<emph\>Field n\</emph\> is the name of a field from the pivot table. \<emph\>Item n\</emph\> is the name of an item from that field.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id6454969				0	kid	8wxd8s‖If the pivot table contains only a single result value that fulfills all of the constraints, or a subtotal result that summarizes all matching values, that result is returned. If there is no matching result, or several ones without a subtotal for them, an error is returned. These conditions apply to results that are included in the pivot table.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id79042				0	kid	b8z085‖If the source data contains entries that are hidden by settings of the pivot table, they are ignored. The order of the Field/Item pairs is not significant. Field and item names are not case-sensitive.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id7928708				0	kid	wy-5a5‖If no constraint for a page field is given, the field's selected value is implicitly used. If a constraint for a page field is given, it must match the field's selected value, or an error is returned. Page fields are the fields at the top left of a pivot table, populated using the "Page Fields" area of the pivot table layout dialog. From each page field, an item (value) can be selected, which means only that item is included in the calculation.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3864253				0	kid	yy8to-‖Subtotal values from the pivot table are only used if they use the function "auto" (except when specified in the constraint, see \<item type=\"literal\"\>Second Syntax\</item\> below).				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144016				0	kid	570lq]‖Second Syntax				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id9937131				0	kid	63gtmk‖            \<emph\>pivot table\</emph\> has the same meaning as in the first syntax.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id5616626				0	kid	qg-okk‖            \<emph\>Constraints\</emph\> is a space-separated list. Entries can be quoted (single quotes). The whole string must be enclosed in quotes (double quotes), unless you reference the string from another cell.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id4076357				0	kid	qhp2j9‖One of the entries can be the data field name. The data field name can be left out if the pivot table contains only one data field, otherwise it must be present.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id8231757				0	kid	cvsg89‖Each of the other entries specifies a constraint in the form \<item type=\"literal\"\>Field[Item]\</item\> (with literal characters [ and ]), or only \<item type=\"literal\"\>Item\</item\> if the item name is unique within all fields that are used in the pivot table.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3168736				0	kid	gv-qz=‖A function name can be added in the form \<emph\>Field[Item;Function]\</emph\>, which will cause the constraint to match only subtotal values which use that function. The possible function names are Sum, Count, Average, Max, Min, Product, Count (Numbers only), StDev (Sample), StDevP (Population), Var (Sample), and VarP (Population), case-insensitive.				20130829 23:02:48
