helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12030200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10637				0	kid	7[5t9k‖ Note for Asian languages: Check \<emph\>Case Sensitivity\</emph\> to apply multi-level collation. With multi-level collation, entries are first compared in their primitive forms with their cases and diacritics ignored. If they evaluate as the same, their diacritics are taken into account for the second-level comparison. If they still evaluate as the same, their cases, character widths, and Japanese Kana difference are considered for the third-level comparison.				20130829 23:02:48
