helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149751	101			0	kid	gvg0r+‖Example				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153982	102			0	kid	ksx6f-‖In the example above (scroll up, please), you can search for the number of children whose name starts with an E or a subsequent letter. Edit the formula in B16 to read \<item type=\"input\"\>=DCOUNTA(A1:E10;"Name";A13:E14)\</item\>. Delete the old search criteria and enter \<item type=\"input\"\>>=E\</item\> under Name in field A14. The result is 5. If you now delete all number values for Greta in row 8, the result changes to 4. Row 8 is no longer included in the count because it does not contain any values. The name Greta is text, not a value. Note that the DatabaseField parameter must point to a column that can contain values.				20130829 23:02:48
