helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148663	25			0	kid	v5g-lm‖\<variable id=\"datapilot_edittable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_edittable.xhp\" name=\"Editing Pivot Tables\"\>Editing Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868	26			0	kid	frzg+5‖Click one of the buttons in the pivot table and hold the mouse button down. A special symbol will appear next to the mouse pointer.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786	27			0	kid	h-ye38‖By dragging the button to a different position in the same row you can alter the order of the columns. If you drag a button to the left edge of the table into the row headings area, you can change a column into a row.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id1648915				0	kid	h+emj[‖In the Pivot Table dialog, you can drag a button to the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area to create a button and a listbox on top of the pivot table. The listbox can be used to filter the pivot table by the contents of the selected item. You can use drag-and-drop within the pivot table to use another page field as a filter.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434	29			0	kid	n0nbky‖To remove a button from the table, just drag it out of the pivot table. Release the mouse button when the mouse pointer positioned within the sheet has become a 'not allowed' icon. The button is deleted.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442	40			0	kid	dvif1+‖To edit the pivot table, click a cell inside the pivot table and open the context menu. In the context menu you find the command \<emph\>Edit Layout\</emph\>, which displays the \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\> dialog for the current pivot table.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id2666096				0	kid	joyohw‖In the pivot table, you can use drag-and-drop or cut/paste commands to rearrange the order of data fields.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id266609688				0	kid	if12xl‖You can assign custom display names to fields, field members, subtotals (with some restrictions), and grand totals inside pivot tables. A custom display name is assigned to an item by overwriting the original name with another name.				20130829 23:02:48
