helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275	14			0	kid	9m]jc0‖The STYLE() function can be added to an existing formula in a cell. For example, together with the CURRENT function, you can color a cell depending on its value. The formula =...+STYLE(IF(CURRENT()>3; "Red"; "Green")) applies the cell style "Red" to cells if the value is greater than 3, otherwise the cell style "Green" is applied.				20130829 23:02:48
