helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id9800103				0	kid	rc0fqr‖If two axes are shown in a bar chart, and some data series are attached to the first axis, while some other data series are attached to the second axis, then both sets of data series are shown independently, overlapping each other.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id2144535				0	kid	e4altm‖As a result, bars attached to the first y-axis are partly or completely hidden by bars attached to the second y-axis. To avoid this, enable the option to display bars side by side. \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The bars from different data series are shown as if they were attached only to one axis.\</ahelp\>				20130829 23:02:48
