helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3341776				0	kid	ybnrqx‖Based on\<emph\> low, high,\</emph\> and \<emph\>close\</emph\> column Type 1 shows an additional horizontal mark \<emph\>for\</emph\> the closing price.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id5947141				0	kid	m68iz7‖Type 2				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id1911679				0	kid	o5+m-2‖Based on \<emph\>open, low, high\</emph\>, and \<emph\>close\</emph\> column Type 2 generates the traditional "candle stick" chart. Type 2 draws the vertical line between the bottom and top price and adds a rectangle in front, which visualizes the range between the opening and closing price. If you click on the rectangle you see more information in the status bar. %PRODUCTNAME uses different fill colors for rising values (the opening price is lower than the closing price) and falling values.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id9364909				0	kid	qscdpa‖Type 3				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4473403				0	kid	gbxb9+‖Based on \<emph\>volume, low, high\</emph\>, and \<emph\>close\</emph\> column chart Type 3 draws a chart like Type 1, with additional columns for the transaction volume.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id4313791				0	kid	gbzy4=‖Type 4				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4331797				0	kid	0iuy93‖Based on all five data columns \<emph\>volume, open, low, high\</emph\>, and \<emph\>close\</emph\>, Type 4 combines a chart of Type 2 with a column chart for the transaction volume.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4191717				0	kid	kdwacy‖Because measurement for transaction volume might be "units", a second y axis is introduced in chart Type 3 and Type 4. The price axis is shown on the right side and the volume axis on the left side.				20130829 23:02:48
