helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751	3			0	kid	zqb8pu‖For $[officename] to support the Java platform, you must install the Java 2 Runtime Environment software. When you installed $[officename], you automatically received the option to install these files if they were not yet installed. You can also install these files now if required.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338	4			0	kid	2iziwa‖The Java platform support needs to be activated under $[officename] to run Java applications.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892	5			0	kid	z-z[oo‖Activate Java platform support by choosing \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/java.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - Java\"\>$[officename] - Java\</link\>\</emph\>.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id9116183				0	kid	aoen8t‖Before you can use a JDBC driver, you need to add its class path. Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME- Java, and click the Class Path button. After you add the path information, restart %PRODUCTNAME.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3153822	11			0	kid	i4emfo‖Your modifications at the \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Java\</emph\> tab page will be used even if the Java Virtual Machine (JVM, a virtual machine for the Java platform) already has been started. After modifications to the ClassPath you must restart $[officename]. The same is true for modifications under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Internet - Proxy\</emph\>. Only the two boxes "Http Proxy" and "Ftp Proxy" and their ports don't require a restart, they will be evaluated when you click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130829 23:02:48
