helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id3149649	29			0	kid	z6+uii‖Documents in OpenDocument file format are stored as compressed zip archives that contain XML files. To view these XML files, you can open the OpenDocument file with an unzip program. The following files and directories are contained within the OpenDocument files:				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id3153178	30			0	kid	u00k64‖The text content of the document is located in \<emph\>content.xml\</emph\>.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id3154068	31			0	kid	ry[1ok‖By default, \<emph\>content.xml\</emph\> is stored without formatting elements like indentation or line breaks to minimize the time for saving and opening the document. On the \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - General\</emph\> tab page you can activate the use of indentations and line breaks by clearing the check box \<emph\>Size optimization for ODF format\</emph\>.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id3145152	32			0	kid	eybmck‖The file \<emph\>meta.xml\</emph\> contains the meta information of the document, which you can enter under \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id3150740	33			0	kid	yq8v57‖If you save a document with a password, \<emph\>meta.xml\</emph\> will not be encrypted.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391	34			0	kid	sk1iwi‖The file \<emph\>settings.xml\</emph\> contains further information about the settings for this document.				20130829 23:02:48
