helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149783	40			0	kid	1jlq23‖By clicking the arrow next to some icons you open a toolbar. To move a toolbar, drag the title bar. As soon as you release the mouse button, the toolbar remains at the new position. Drag the title bar to another position, or drag to an edge of the window, where the toolbar will dock. Close a toolbar by clicking the Close Window icon. Make the toolbar visible again by choosing \<emph\>View - Toolbars - (toolbar name)\</emph\>.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152414	79			0	kid	m0k]2j‖Spin button				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id1094088				0	kid	esec9h‖In form controls, a spin button is a property of a numerical field, currency field, date field, or time field. If the property "Spin button" is enabled, the field shows a pair of symbols with arrows pointing to opposing directions, either vertically or horizontally.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id7493209				0	kid	7sjf6x‖In the Basic IDE, a spin button is the name used for the numerical field together with the two arrow symbols.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155599	78			0	kid	d5atzf‖You can type a numerical value into the field next to the spin button, or select the value with the up-arrow or down-arrow symbols on the spin button. On the keyboard you can press the up arrow and down arrow keys to increase or reduce the value. You can press the Page Up and Page Down keys to set the maximum and minimum value.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150264	38			0	kid	wdxi=6‖If the field next to the spin button defines numerical values, you can also define a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000003.xhp#metrik\" name=\"measurement unit\"\>measurement unit\</link\>, for example, 1 cm or 5 mm, 12 pt or 2".				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154232	76			0	kid	f228=1‖Convert				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148983	77			0	kid	4lgwo1‖\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you click forward through the dialog, this button is called \<emph\>Next\</emph\>. On the last page the button has the name \<emph\>Convert\</emph\>. The conversion is then performed by clicking the button.\</ahelp\>				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145129	42			0	kid	t3i9kx‖Context Menu				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156553	44			0	kid	4i9w=w‖\<variable id=\"context\"\>To activate the context menu of an object, first click the object with the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>left\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> mouse button to select it, and then, \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>while holding down the Ctrl key or the Command and Option keys, click the mouse button again\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\> click the right mouse button\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>. Some context menus can be called even if the object has not been selected. Context menus are found just about everywhere in $[officename].\</variable\>				20130829 23:02:48
