helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148481	100			0	kid	0z20hc‖In this case, standard formatting is formatting that refers to the internally stored data. It is not always visible to the user, especially if it is used for simulating data types (for example, time fields in dBASE databases). This depends on the database used and the individual data type. Searching with field formatting is appropriate if you only want to find what is actually shown. This includes fields of type Date, Time, Date/Time and Number/Double.				20130829 23:02:48
