helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3148773	64			0	kid	a7fahv‖For forms with database links, the associated database is defined in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170200.xhp\" name=\"Form Properties\"\>Form Properties\</link\>. You will find the functions for this on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"Data\"\>\<emph\>Data\</emph\>\</link\> tab page.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377	65			0	kid	bj4pex‖The possible settings of the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab page of a control depend on the respective control. You will only see the options that are available for the current control and context. The following fields are available:				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108B4				0	kid	y73q+2‖Reference value (off)				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN108B8				0	kid	nd[lby‖\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Check boxes and radio buttons in spreadsheets can be bound to cells in the current document. If the control is enabled, the value you enter in Reference value (on) is copied to the cell. If the control is disabled, the value from Reference value (off) is copied to the cell.\</ahelp\>				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159121	71			0	kid	gslv9f‖Reference value (on)				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3163812	141			0	kid	ao0c4w‖\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_REFVALUE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>You can enter a reference value for the web form, which will be remitted to a server when sending the form. With database forms, the value entered is written in the database field, assigned to the control field.\</ahelp\>You can assign a reference value to option buttons and check boxes. The reference value will be remitted to a server when sending the web form. With database forms the value entered here will be written in the database assigned to the control field.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150225	204			0	kid	6dx+-i‖\<emph\>Reference values for web forms\</emph\>				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3147611	205			0	kid	6u3d+d‖Reference values are useful if you design a web form and the information on the status of the control is to be transmitted to a server. If the control is clicked by the user, the corresponding reference value is sent to the server.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3149570	194			0	kid	b-n2jh‖For example, if you have two control fields for the options "feminine" and "masculine", and assign a reference value of 1 to the field "feminine" and the value 2 to the "masculine" field, the value 1 is transmitted to the server if a user clicks the "feminine" field and value 2 is sent if the "masculine" field is clicked.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150260	206			0	kid	+xcoe-‖\<emph\>Reference values for database forms\</emph\>				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150654	207			0	kid	vgm83n‖For database forms, you can also characterize the status of an option or a check box by a reference value, storing it in the database. If you have a set of three options, for example "in progress", "completed", and "resubmission", with the respective reference values, "ToDo", "OK", and "RS", these reference values appear in the database if the respective option is clicked.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148455	5			0	kid	okk2ip‖Data field				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155852	6			0	kid	26[gew‖\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CONTROLSOURCE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the field of the data source table to which the control refers.\</ahelp\>With database forms, you can link controls with the data fields.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153224	75			0	kid	lqip51‖You have several possibilities:				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3159110	66			0	kid	m[7[r6‖First case: There is only one table in the form.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3156356	67			0	kid	4qheuc‖Under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>, specify the field of the data source table whose contents you want to be displayed.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3146898	76			0	kid	v25xec‖Second case: The control belongs to a subform that is created by an SQL query.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154273	77			0	kid	riz4bh‖Under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>, specify the field of the SQL statement whose contents you want to be displayed.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153949	78			0	kid	4n541c‖Third case: \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"Combo Boxes\"\>Combo Boxes\</link\>				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3147494	79			0	kid	x-6j[u‖For combo boxes, the field of the data source table in which the values entered or selected by the user should be stored is specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>. The values displayed in the list of the combo box are based on an SQL statement, which is entered under \<emph\>List content\</emph\>.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145167	68			0	kid	a30p77‖Fourth case: \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"List Boxes\"\>List Boxes\</link\>				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153764	91			0	kid	ty3zz8‖The data source table does not contain the data to be displayed, but rather a table linked to the data source table through a common data field.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3149021	69			0	kid	b5byh9‖If you want a list box to display data from a table that is linked to the current data source table, under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\> specify the field of the data source table to which the content of the list box refers. Or you can specify the database field that controls the display of the data in the form. This data field provides the link to the other table if both tables can be linked through a common data field. It is usually a data field in which unique identification numbers are stored. The data field whose contents are displayed in the form is specified by an SQL statement under \<emph\>List content\</emph\>.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153924	80			0	kid	lx-3yr‖List boxes work with references. They can either be implemented with linked tables by SQL statements (fourth case) or through value lists:				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145641	58			0	kid	4356kh‖\<emph\>References through linked tables (SQL statements)\</emph\>				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3147341	59			0	kid	h[+[ej‖If you want a list box to display data from a database table that is linked by a common data field to the table on which the form is based, the link field of the form table is specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3155174	60			0	kid	j8jf+v‖The link is created with an SQL Select, which, if you selected "SQL" or "Native SQL", is specified under \<emph\>Type of list contents\</emph\> in the field \<emph\>List content\</emph\>. As an example, a table "Orders" is linked to the current form control, and in the database a table "Customers" is linked to the "Orders" table. You can use an SQL statement as follows:				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3148537	70			0	kid	usv1av‖SELECT CustomerName, CustomerNo FROM Customers,				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154967	71			0	kid	vl563+‖where "CustomerName" is the data field from the linked table "Customers", and "CustomerNo" is the field of the table "Customers" that is linked to a field of the form table "Orders" specified under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3163808	55			0	kid	o0t[8=‖\<emph\>References Using Value Lists\</emph\>				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145295	56			0	kid	f6qpf2‖For list boxes, you can use value lists. Value lists are lists that define reference values. In this way, the control in the form does not directly display the content of a database field, but rather values assigned in the value list.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3151186	57			0	kid	g=zogb‖If you work with reference values of a value list, the contents of the data field that you specified under \<emph\>Data Field\</emph\> in the form are not visible, but rather the assigned values. If you chose "Valuelist" on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab under \<emph\>Type of list contents\</emph\> and assigned a reference value to the visible list entries in the form under \<emph\>List entries\</emph\> (entered in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"General\"\>\<emph\>General\</emph\>\</link\> tab), then the reference values are compared with the data content of the given data field. If a reference value corresponds to the content of a data field, the associated list entries are displayed in the form.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154664	3			0	kid	r=nfpr‖Bound field				20130829 23:02:48
