helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AD2				0	kid	f[1fhj‖If you delete the contents of the \<emph\>Bound field\</emph\> cell in the property browser, the first field of the result set is used to display and to exchange data.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3154588	72			0	kid	6l[r-n‖This property for list boxes defines which data field of a linked table is displayed in the form.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3151213	38			0	kid	2i22yd‖If a list box in the form is to display contents of a table linked to the form table, then define in the \<emph\>Type of list contents\</emph\> field if the display is determined by an SQL command or the (linked) table is accessed. With the \<emph\>Bound field\</emph\> property, you use an index to specify to which data field of the query or of the table the list field is linked. 				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3148427	73			0	kid	rcuu7u‖The property \<emph\>Bound field\</emph\> is only for forms that are used to access more than one table. If the form is based on only one table, the field to be displayed in the form is specified directly under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>. However, if you want the list box to display data from a table that is linked to the current table over a common data field, the linked data field is defined by the property \<emph\>Bound field\</emph\>.				20130829 23:02:48
