helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153139	20			0	kid	9bxv92‖\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATAENTRY\"\>Determines if the form only allows the addition of new data (Yes) or if it allows other properties as well (No).\</ahelp\>				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575	21			0	kid	6dls[f‖If \<emph\>Add data only\</emph\> is set to "Yes", changing or deleting data is not possible.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148455	9			0	kid	fogteq‖Navigation bar				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3157976	22			0	kid	t2l+t9‖\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_NAVIGATION\"\>Specifies whether the navigation functions in the lower form bar can be used.\</ahelp\>				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149485	79			0	kid	9acceu‖The "Parent Form" option is used for subforms. If you choose this option for a subform, you can navigate using the records of the main form if the cursor is placed in the subform. A subform is linked to the parent form by a 1:1 relationship, so navigation is always performed in the parent form.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151051	10			0	kid	n7vp]w‖Cycle				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944	23			0	kid	kggpmv‖\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CYCLE\"\>Determines how the navigation should be done using the tab key.\</ahelp\> Using the tab key, you can move forward in the form. If you simultaneously press the Shift key, the navigation will follow the opposite direction. If you reach the last (or the first) field and press the tab key again, it can have various effects. Define the key control with the following options:				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3166413	87			0	kid	zn0i49‖Option				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150424	88			0	kid	atsk6z‖Meaning				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150417	89			0	kid	+obkw1‖Default				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3157847	90			0	kid	64fh=u‖This setting automatically defines a cycle which follows an existing database link: If the form contains a database link, the Tab key will, by default, initiate a change to the next or previous record on exit from the last field (see All Records). If there is no database link the next/previous form is shown (see Current Page).				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418	91			0	kid	i[f=6t‖All records				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3152972	92			0	kid	t[do2+‖This option applies to database forms only and is used to navigate through all records. If you use the Tab key to exit from the last field of a form, the current record is changed.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3151020	93			0	kid	zr8-qe‖Active record				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3145301	94			0	kid	lea3-e‖This option applies to database forms only, and is used to navigate within the current record. If you use the Tab key to exit from the last field of a form, the current record is changed.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3146913	95			0	kid	uc]90r‖Current page				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150330	96			0	kid	t]f9zs‖On exit from the last field of a form, the cursor skips to the first field in the next form. This is standard for HTML forms; therefore, this option is especially relevant for HTML forms.				20130829 23:02:48
