helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152570	136			0	kid	okrkf2‖In $[officename] you do not need any knowledge of SQL for most queries, since you do not have to enter the SQL code. If you create a query in the query design, $[officename] automatically converts your instructions into the corresponding SQL syntax. If, with the help of the \<emph\>Switch Design View On/Off \</emph\>button, you change to the SQL view, you can see the SQL commands for a query that has been created previously.				20130829 23:02:48
