helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145649	265			0	kid	dao7b4‖On the \<emph\>Device\</emph\> tab page, you can activate the special options for your printer. If your printer can only print in black and white, choose "grayscale" under \<emph\>Color\</emph\>, otherwise choose "color". If switching to grayscale leads to unfavorable results, you can also select "color" under \<emph\>Color\</emph\> and see how the printer or PostScript emulator applies it. Furthermore, on this tab page you can set the precision with which colors are described as well as the PostScript level.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752	284			0	kid	9=]13[‖The \<emph\>Font Replacement\</emph\> tab page allows you to select a printer font type available in the printer for each font type installed on your computer. This way you can reduce the data volume sent to the printer. Font replacement can be turned on or off for each printer individually.				20130829 23:02:48
