helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093D				0	kid	stf9h+‖An XML filter contains \<emph\>stylesheets\</emph\> that are written in the XSLT language. The stylesheets define the transformation from the OpenDocument file format to another XML format through export and import filters. There are three types of XML filters:				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10947				0	kid	20ml-q‖ \<emph\>Import Filters\</emph\> load external XML files and transform the format of the files into the OpenDocument XML file format. After you install an import filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\>.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10960				0	kid	y0+axk‖ \<emph\>Export Filters\</emph\> transform OpenDocument XML files and \<emph\>save\</emph\> the files to a different XML format. After you install an export filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070001.xhp\"\>Export dialog\</link\>.				20130829 23:02:48
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10979				0	kid	oszgdz‖ \<emph\>Import/Export Filters\</emph\> load and save OpenDocument XML files into a different XML \<emph\>format\</emph\>. After you install these filters, the names of the filters are added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\> and the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\"\>File Save As dialog\</link\>.				20130829 23:02:48
