helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154906	50			0	kid	nqwts6‖To change the size of a formula, use "size +" or -,*,/. Do not use "size n". These can easily be used in any context. This enables you to copy to other areas by using Copy and Paste, and the result remains the same. Furthermore, such expressions survive a change of base size in the menu better than when using "size n". If you use only "size *" and "size /" (for example, "size *1.24 a or size /0.86 a") the proportions remain intact.				20130829 23:02:48
