readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	Linuxi3a	Linuxi3a			0	kid	phf]z[‖There is a wide variety of Linux distributions, and even within the same distribution there may be different installation options (KDE vs Gnome, etc.). Some distributions ship with their own ‘native’ version of ${PRODUCTNAME}, which may have different features from this Community ${PRODUCTNAME}. Sometimes you can install the Community ${PRODUCTNAME} alongside the ‘native’ version. However, it’s usually safer to remove the ‘native’ version before installing this Community version. Consult the documentation for your distribution for details of how to do this.				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	Linuxi4a	Linuxi4a			0	kid	bjbg5d‖It is recommended that you always backup your system before you remove or install software.				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	Precautions	Precautions			0	kid	lnf1b3‖Please make sure you have enough free memory in the temporary directory on your system and that read, write and run access rights have been granted. Close all other programs before starting the installation.				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	naso01	naso01			0	kid	sr[tk6‖Problems During Program Startup				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	naso02	naso02			0	kid	6zccv[‖If you experience ${PRODUCTNAME} startup problems (most notably while using Gnome) please 'unset' the <tt>SESSION_MANAGER</tt> environment variable inside the shell you use to start ${PRODUCTNAME}. This can be done by adding the line "<tt>unset SESSION_MANAGER</tt>" to the beginning of the soffice shell script found in the "<tt>[office folder]/program</tt>" directory.				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	abcdef	abcdef			0	kid	gcvsx=‖Difficulties starting ${PRODUCTNAME} (e.g. applications hang) as well as problems with the screen display are often caused by the graphics card driver. If these problems occur, please update your graphics card driver or try using the graphics driver delivered with your operating system. Difficulties displaying 3D objects can often be solved by deactivating the option "Use OpenGL" under 'Tools - Options - ${PRODUCTNAME} - View - 3D view'.				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	naso	naso			0	kid	wtzny[‖ALPS/Synaptics notebook touchpads in Windows				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	naso2	naso2			0	kid	yo32tt‖Due to a Windows driver issue, you cannot scroll through ${PRODUCTNAME} documents when you slide your finger across an ALPS/Synaptics touchpad.				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	naso6	naso6			0	kid	q45rq9‖To enable touchpad scrolling, add the following lines to the "<tt>C:\Program Files\Synaptics\SynTP\SynTPEnh.ini</tt>" configuration file, and restart your computer:				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	naso8	naso8			0	kid	h5yras‖The location of the configuration file might vary on different versions of Windows.				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	sdfsd32asrc	sdfsd32asrc			0	kid	x0c4]8‖Mozilla Address Book Driver				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	sdcc32asrc	sdcc32asrc			0	kid	4v=371‖The Mozilla address book driver requires the <tt>SUNWzlib</tt> package. This package is not part of the minimum Solaris operating system installation. If you require access to the Mozilla address book, then add this package to your Solaris operating system using the command "<tt>pkgadd</tt>" from the installation CD.				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	awe1	awe1			0	kid	t7=hte‖Shortcut Keys				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	w32e1	w32e1			0	kid	ktbu0s‖Only shortcut keys (key combinations) not used by the operating system can be used in ${PRODUCTNAME}. If a key combination in ${PRODUCTNAME} does not work as described in the ${PRODUCTNAME} Help, check if that shortcut is already used by the operating system. To rectify such conflicts, you can change the keys assigned by your operating system. Alternatively, you can change almost any key assignment in ${PRODUCTNAME}. For more information on this topic, refer to the ${PRODUCTNAME} Help or the Help documentation of your operating system.				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	mackeys1	mackeys1			0	kid	dkho27‖The application help of ${PRODUCTNAME} may use shortcut combinations for PC keyboards only.				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	gfh6w	gfh6w			0	kid	4k1wrs‖File Locking				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	pji76w	pji76w			0	kid	iidzw7‖File locking is enabled by default in ${PRODUCTNAME}. On a network that uses the Network File System protocol (NFS), the locking daemon for NFS clients must be active. To disable file locking, edit the <tt>soffice</tt> script and change the line "<tt>export SAL_ENABLE_FILE_LOCKING</tt>" to "<tt># export SAL_ENABLE_FILE_LOCKING</tt>". If you disable file locking, the write access of a document is not restricted to the user who first opens the document.				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	pji76wsdf	pji76wsdf			0	kid	-2abe7‖Warning: The activated file locking feature can cause problems with Solaris 2.5.1 and 2.7 used in conjunction with Linux NFS 2.0. If your system environment has these parameters, we strongly recommend that you avoid using the file locking feature. Otherwise, ${PRODUCTNAME} will hang when you try to open a file from a NFS mounted directory from a Linux computer.				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	gfh6w1	gfh6w1			0	kid	c+b4mz‖Problems When Sending Documents as E-mails From ${PRODUCTNAME}				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	pji76w1	pji76w1			0	kid	hpvwla‖When sending a document via 'File - Send - Document as E-mail' or 'Document as PDF Attachment' problems might occur (program crashes or hangs). This is due to the Windows system file "Mapi" (Messaging Application Programming Interface) which causes problems in some file versions. Unfortunately, the problem cannot be narrowed down to a certain version number. For more information visit <a href="http://www.microsoft.com">http://www.microsoft.com</a> to search the Microsoft Knowledge Base for "mapi dll".				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	aw22	aw22			0	kid	0y0n4+‖Important Accessibility Notes				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	access7	access7			0	kid	j7hq+s‖For more information on the accessibility features in ${PRODUCTNAME}, see <a href="http://www.openoffice.org/access/">http://www.openoffice.org/access/</a>				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	support	support			0	kid	yh6c4k‖User Support				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	support1	support1			0	kid	a7e]2j‖The main support page <a href="http://support.openoffice.org/">http://support.openoffice.org/</a> offers various possibilities for help with ${PRODUCTNAME}. Your question may have already been answered - check the Community Forum at <a href="http://forum.openoffice.org">http://forum.openoffice.org</a> or search the archives of the 'users@openoffice.apache.org' mailing list at <a href="http://openoffice.apache.org/mailing-lists.html">http://openoffice.apache.org/mailing-lists.html</a>. Alternatively, you can send in your questions to <a href="mailto:users@openoffice.apache.org">users@openoffice.apache.org</a>. How to subscribe to the list (to get an email response) is explained on this page: <a href="http://openoffice.apache.org/mailing-lists.html">http://openoffice.apache.org/mailing-lists.html</a>.				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	faq	faq			0	kid	s[aqyy‖Also check the FAQ section at <a href="http://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/FAQ">http://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/FAQ</a>.				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	reportbugs	reportbugs			0	kid	pt8kni‖Reporting Bugs &amp; Issues				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	reportbugs1	reportbugs1			0	kid	nik44f‖The ${PRODUCTNAME} Web site hosts <a href="https://issues.apache.org/ooo/">BugZilla</a>, our mechanism for reporting, tracking and solving bugs and issues. We encourage all users to feel entitled and welcome to report issues that may arise on your particular platform. Energetic reporting of issues is one of the most important contributions that the user community can make to the ongoing development and improvement of the suite.				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	gettinginvolved1	gettinginvolved1			0	kid	4wf[v+‖Getting Involved				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	gettinginvolved2	gettinginvolved2			0	kid	kh2k-n‖The ${PRODUCTNAME} Community would very much benefit from your active participation in the development of this important open source project.				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	gettingimvolved3	gettingimvolved3			0	kid	ppvrmc‖As a user, you are already a valuable part of the suite's development process and we would like to encourage you to take an even more active role with a view to being a long-term contributor to the community. Please join and check out the user page at <a href="http://openoffice.apache.org/get-involved.html">http://openoffice.apache.org/get-involved.html</a>				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	howtostart	howtostart			0	kid	y8k48m‖How to Start				20130829 23:02:48
readlicense_oo	docs\readme\readme.xrm	0	readmeitem	howtostart1	howtostart1			0	kid	tfp6km‖The best way to start contributing is to subscribe to one or more of the mailing lists, lurk for a while, and gradually use the mail archives to familiarize yourself with many of the topics covered since the ${PRODUCTNAME} source code was released back in October 2000. When you're comfortable, all you need to do is send an email self-introduction and jump right in.				20130829 23:02:48
