swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id8654133				0	kid	lk2in4‖The following list gives an overview of the text formats that the @WIKIEXTENSIONPRODUCTNAME@ can upload to the Wiki server.				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id5630664				0	kid	3]k6o8‖The OpenDocument format used by Writer and the WikiMedia format are quite different. Only a subset of all features can be transformed from one format to the other.				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id7178868				0	kid	mi2db-‖Headings				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id508133				0	kid	ftfsjz‖Apply a heading paragraph style to the headings in your Writer document. The Wiki will show the heading styles of the same outline level, formatted as defined by the Wiki engine.				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id7217627				0	kid	0r[=-d‖Hyperlinks				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id3735465				0	kid	o5czy2‖Native OpenDocument hyperlinks are transformed into "external" Wiki links. Therefore, the built-in linking facility of OpenDocument should only be used to create links that point to other sites outside the Wiki web. For creating Wiki links that point to other subjects of the same Wiki domain, use Wiki links.				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id941190				0	kid	jw9w30‖Lists				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id8942838				0	kid	2]qsos‖Lists can reliably be exported when the whole list uses a consistent list style. Use the Numbering or Bullets icon to generate a list in Writer. If you need a list without numbering or bullets, use Format - Bullets and Numbering to define and apply the respective list style.				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id7026886				0	kid	tes]f9‖Paragraphs				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id4436475				0	kid	ct]oi=‖Alignment				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id376598				0	kid	9ujpx1‖Explicit text alignment should not be used in Wiki articles. Nevertheless, text alignment is supported for left, centered, and right alignment of text.				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id7486190				0	kid	8d+i+o‖Pre-formatted text				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id1459395				0	kid	0v9p+-‖A paragraph style with a fixed-width font is transformed as pre-formatted text. Pre-formatted text is shown on the Wiki with a border around the text.				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id4834131				0	kid	1wx-c8‖Character styles				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id6397595				0	kid	b-4nbn‖Character styles modify the appearance of parts of a paragraph. The transformation supports bold, italics, bold/italics, subscript and superscript. All fixed width fonts are transformed into the Wiki typewriter style.				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id5152745				0	kid	09+4n9‖Footnotes				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id5238196				0	kid	9f[zro‖Note: The transformation uses the new style of footnotes with <ref> and <references> tags that requires the Cite.php extension to be installed into MediaWiki. If those tags occur as plain text in the transformation result, ask the Wiki administrator to install this extension.				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id9405499				0	kid	xr+c5+‖Images				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id3541673				0	kid	53lqe[‖Images cannot be exported by a transformation producing a single file of Wiki text. However, if the image is already uploaded to the target Wiki domain (e. g. WikiMedia Commons), then the transformation produces a valid image tag that includes the image. Image captions are also supported.				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id2162236				0	kid	mx-0qg‖Tables				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id3037202				0	kid	l3al0l‖Simple tables are supported well. Table headers are translated into corresponding Wiki style table headers. However, custom formatting of table borders, column sizes and background colors is ignored.				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id2954496				0	kid	ctemb3‖Joined Cells				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id8253730				0	kid	t2=7lf‖OpenDocument and especially OpenOffice.org represent tables that have joined cells that span rows as tables with nested tables. In contrast, the wiki model of table is to declare column and row spans for such joined cells. 				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id8163090				0	kid	5z8u-3‖If only columns of the same row are joined, the result of the transformation resembles the source document very well.				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id425122				0	kid	lu2n7b‖Borders				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id1831110				0	kid	dgnnwj‖Irrespective of custom table styles for border and background, a table is always exported as "\<emph\>prettytable"\</emph\>, which renders in the Wiki engine with simple borders and bold header.				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	hd_id6255073				0	kid	fb9jxm‖Charset and special characters				20130829 23:02:48
swext	mediawiki\help\wikiformats.xhp	0	help	par_id8216193				0	kid	k]h[ro‖The charset of the transformation result is fixed to UTF-8. Depending on your system, this might not be the default charset. This might cause "special characters" to look broken when viewed with default settings. However, you can switch your editor to UTF-8 encoding to fix this. If your editor does not support switching the encoding, you can display the result of the transformation in the Firefox browser and switch the encoding to UTF-8 there. Now, you can cut and paste the transformation result to your program of choice.				20130829 23:02:48
